text:
A minimal reproducible benchmark needs:
1. the exact data set (include a public URL or SHA-256 hash);
2. a deterministic loading/generation step;
3. the metric code under test;
4. a fixed seed for any randomness;
5. hardware info (cores, memory, turbo mode);
6. software versions (`pip freeze` or `conda list`).
Report the result with a 95 % confidence interval over 10 runs; variability often teaches more than the mean alone.

