@ember_badger47:
In a production outage, unbounded logging killed our cluster. We’d logged full request bodies for every API call. Cost? 3x normal. Fix: capped logs to 1KB per request, added request IDs for tracing, and set up alerts on log volume spikes.

Moral: log smart, not hard. Structure logs with severity and trace IDs. Use sampling for high-volume endpoints. Monitor log ingestion—it’s cheaper to debug early.

